  "shared_bindings": [
    "Current mode/type/depth reuse the actual existing cells;type snapshot has the native signed BYTE view while its owner stays BYTE. Pending and input gate reuse host_startup_storage fields,not duplicate old-address globals.",
    "Music/sound BYTEs and extraDWORD access reuse registry_config[72]at offsets13/14/16. DWORD physical view is measured for this historical source/toolchain;original struct/type and universal alias behavior are unproved.",
    "Display request,fullscreen/window owner,reset state,priority/audio controls,MCI state,bank/channel/loop/counter/scratch providers all use their actual canonical owners.",
    "Old graphics-named CD/sound callback declarations now bind directly to actual 9D60/9DB0/9F60/FFB0/10010/10030 providers by address and cdecl view. No duplicate callback bodies or production stubs."
  ],
  "behavior": [
    "Null window returns before cache changes. If all seven cache fields match,return before testing dirty flags;dirty flags alone do not break the initial cache guard.",
    "First two cached bytes are compared as unsigned lowBYTE against sign-extended requested mode/type;depth/extra use fullDWORD,other cache flags useBYTE. Negative mode/type views therefore retain original repeated-transition behavior.",
    "Nonzero initial depth sets actual pending/resetDWORDs1. Choose active/waiting branch from captured initial mode/type/depth. Active title depends on current input gate;actual sound/CD on/off callbacks run when corresponding dirty or registry/cache mismatch permits.",
    "Waiting path sets the native title,executes actual display-mode setter and suspension/priority path,then reloads live depth before sound pause and live mode/type before CD pause. Final cache capture reloads current global/registry values after callbacks.",
    "Preserve callback order,ignored API returns,native window-title bytes and opaque cache padding. The measured cache/type views do not assign original variable names or exact state meanings."
  ],
